docs {
  Real-world snap-complete query, mirroring a HouseholdDeterminationRequest
  from the partner team's eligibility-adapter contract.

  Body lifted verbatim from data/factgraph/snap-complete/profiles.json
  ("Default" profile) with the member id set to "head" — that's our
  canonical working scenario. Single applicant, 35 years old, US
  citizen, head of household, $1,200/month wages from a 30-hour-per-week
  compensated job, $800/month rent, $500 in a checking account.

  Verified response (against prod 2026-05-27):

      "status": "complete",
      "values": {
        "/isExpedited":         false,
        "/eligibilityCategory": "Ece",
        "/allotment":           221,
        "/proratedAllotment":   192
      }

  Maps to ProgramDecision:
    - status: "approved"     (Ece is one of three eligible categories;
                              see Bce, Ece, Se)
    - path:   "auto"

  See packages/factgraph-api/docs/examples-snap.md for the
  field-by-field mapping from a HouseholdDeterminationRequest to
  this body, plus variations (expedited screening, denial with
  denialReasonCode, multi-member).
}
